{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 427381, "name": "Vinme", "username": "kan3da9", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/51a2da/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-08-09T15:57:21.204Z", "cooked": "<p>Hey, so basically i have KDE spin of fedora (42), but decided to migrate to COSMIC instead and I want to replace the KDE-specific packages with generic/workstation (or COSMIC) equivalents and then remove all KDE packages.</p>\n<p>When i try the usual approach: <code>sudo dnf remove \"*kde*\" \"*plasma*\" \"*kf5*\" \"*kf6*\"</code> , I get dependency conflicts with system-release packages:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">Failed to resolve the transaction:\nProblem 1: installed package setup-2.15.0-13.fc42.noarch requires system-release, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - conflicting requests\n  - problem with installed package\n Problem 2: installed package setup-2.15.0-13.fc42.noarch requires system-release, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - installed package fedora-release-kde-42-28.noarch requires fedora-release-common = 42-28, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - installed package pam-1.7.0-6.fc42.x86_64 requires setup, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - installed package fedora-release-common-42-28.noarch requires fedora-release-identity = 42-28, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - installed package sudo-1.9.17-2.p1.fc42.x86_64 requires pam, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - conflicting requests\n  - problem with installed package\n</code></pre>\n<p>Current fedora release packages are:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">fedora-release-identity-kde-42-28.noarch\nfedora-release-kde-42-28.noarch\nfedora-release-common-42-28.noarch\n</code></pre>\n<p>I also tried swapping the release packages first:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">Updating and loading repositories:\nRepositories loaded.\nFailed to resolve the transaction:\nProblem: problem with installed package\n  - package fedora-release-identity-kde-42-25.noarch from fedora requires fedora-release-kde = 42-25, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - installed package fedora-release-identity-kde-42-28.noarch requires fedora-release-kde = 42-28, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - package fedora-release-identity-kde-42-28.noarch from updates requires fedora-release-kde = 42-28, but none of the providers can be installed\n  - conflicting requests\n</code></pre>\n<p>So basically <strong>What’s the proper way to replace <code>fedora-release-kde</code> and <code>fedora-release-identity-kde</code> with their generic equivalents so I can then safely remove all KDE packages?</strong></p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2025-08-09T15:57:21.204Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1243, "reads": 31, "readers_count": 30, "score": 6206.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 161943, "topic_slug": "how-to-remove-kde-packages-from-fedora-kde-spin-when-using-different-de-cosmic", "display_username": "Vinme", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28729, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/how-to-remove-kde-packages-from-fedora-kde-spin-when-using-different-de-cosmic/161943/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 427384, "name": "Vinme", "username": "kan3da9", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/51a2da/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-08-09T16:02:24.880Z", "cooked": "<p>Okay, apparently there is similar thread here:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"77776\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/aad0ee/48.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/uninstall-kde-group/77776\">Uninstall KDE group</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ask/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #38BC3B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"Have questions? Get answers here! Ask anything about installing, using, troubleshooting, customizing, or upgrading any variant of Fedora Linux.\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">Ask Fedora</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    Hi all, \nI tried to remove KDE with \nsudo dnf groupremove \" KDE (K Desktop Environment \" \nAnd sudo dnf remove @kde-desktop \nBut it says plasma-desktop is protected and add --skip-broken but even with that option added it won’t remove KDE\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n\n<p><code>sudo dnf swap fedora-release*kde fedora-release-cosmic</code> swapped the release.</p>\n<p>but, running <code>sudo dnf remove \"*kde*\" \"*plasma*\" \"*kf5*\" \"*kf6*\"</code> gives me:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">Failed to resolve the transaction:\nProblem: The operation would result in removing the following protected packages: cosmic-session\n</code></pre>\n<p>Im so confused.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2025-08-09T16:02:24.880Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 118, "reads": 28, "readers_count": 27, "score": 600.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 161943, "topic_slug": "how-to-remove-kde-packages-from-fedora-kde-spin-when-using-different-de-cosmic", "display_username": "Vinme", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/uninstall-kde-group/77776", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Uninstall KDE group", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 28729, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/how-to-remove-kde-packages-from-fedora-kde-spin-when-using-different-de-cosmic/161943/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 427390, "name": "Brian Allenby", "username": "brianallenby", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-08-09T16:17:08.483Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"kan3da9\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"161943\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/k/51a2da/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Vinme:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Im so confused.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Uninstalling those packages and their ilk, will uninstall something that cosmic-session relies on and subsequently pull cosmic-session too.</p>\n<p>If for example I was switching between GNOME and KDE, I would drop to a <code>tty</code> and do the following on the command line:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\"># DISABLE SDDM.\nsudo systemctl disable sddm.service\n\n# Remove KDE environment\nsudo dnf remove @kde-desktop sddm*\n\n# REMOVE ANY LEFTOVER KDE SOFTWARE.\nsudo dnf remove plasma* kf5* kf6*\n\n# REMOVE ANY ORPHANED PACKAGES.\nsudo dnf autoremove\n</code></pre>\n<p>Then I’d install GNOME.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\"># INSTALL GNOME DESKTOP\nsudo dnf install @workstation-product\n\n# ENABLE GDM LOGIN MANAGER.\nsudo systemctl set-default graphical-target \nsudo systemctl enable gdm.service\n</code></pre>\n<p>Then I’d delete all the dot files and dot folders I didn’t want to create a “clean” environment while retaining the XDG dirs from documents, downloads, et cetera.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">rm -rf .cache .config .local .mozilla (or whatever I didn't want leaving behind crap)\n</code></pre>\n<p>After that I’d reboot with…</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo systemctl reboot\n</code></pre>\n<p>I have used the <code>swap</code> option before when it comes to DE changes and to be honest, I prefer the scorched earth policy of just tearing the original DE I was using out by the roots, purging the /home folder and installing the new DE.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2025-08-09T16:25:53.247Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 95, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 495.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 161943, "topic_slug": "how-to-remove-kde-packages-from-fedora-kde-spin-when-using-different-de-cosmic", "display_username": "Brian Allenby", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "fl